*  WAS SRDL R0,8. R0 ARRIVES AS A PAGE COUNT AND LEAVES AS A   XA0034DK         
*  COUNT OF 64-BYTE UNITS, WHICH IS WHAT STL COUNTS AND WHAT   XA0034DK         
*  00262000 STORES AFTER A BCTR. THE PROJECT'S OWN CARDS       XA0034DK         
*  SETTLE THE UNITS: 00249000 DOES LR R7,R3 AND 00250000 SLL   XA0034DK         
*  R7,6 -- TIMES 64 BYTES PER TABLE -- AND 00222500 READS LA   XA0034DK         
*  R1,1(,R1) SEGMENT COUNT/16.                                 XA0034DK         
*  A 64-BYTE UNIT IS SIXTEEN FULLWORD STES IN BOTH             XA0034DK         
*  ARCHITECTURES, BECAUSE AN STE IS A FULLWORD IN BOTH. WHAT   XA0034DK         
*  MOVED IS WHAT SIXTEEN ENTRIES COVER: 16 TIMES 64 KB IS 1    XA0034DK         
*  MB, 16 TIMES 1 MB IS 16 MB. SO THE SAME TABLE LENGTH NOW    XA0034DK         
*  SPANS SIXTEEN TIMES THE ADDRESS SPACE AND THE SHIFT THAT    XA0034DK         
*  DIVIDES PAGES BY A UNIT GROWS BY FOUR. IT IS WRITTEN 8+4    XA0034DK         
*  BECAUSE 00222700 IS ITS EXACT INVERSE, SLL R1,4+8.          XA0034DK         
*  DMKVAT'S OWN GEOMETRY TABLE IS THE CITATION. CODEB0 --      XA0034DK         
*  LARGE PAGE, LARGE SEG, FULLWORD ENTRIES, WHICH IS THIS      XA0034DK         
*  ARCHITECTURE -- CARRIES PAGINCR H'64', THE UNIT, AND        XA0034DK         
*  MAXSEGS H'127', A SEVEN-BIT STL. 128 UNITS OF 16 MB IS 2    XA0034DK         
*  GB, WHICH IS THE WHOLE 31-BIT SPACE, SO THE FIELD IS WIDE   XA0034DK         
*  ENOUGH AND ONLY THIS SHIFT WAS WRONG.                       XA0034DK         
         SRDL  R0,8+4         SHIFT TO OBTAIN NUMBER OF UNITS  XA0034DK         
./ R 00215000          $ 00215100 100                                           
         IC    R4,VMSEG+3     STL IS BITS 25-31 NOW, NOT 0-7   XA0034DK         
         N     R4,=A(SEGSTLM) WITHOUT THE S BIT                XA0034DK         
./ R 00222300          $ 00222310 010                                           
         IC    R1,VMSEG+3     STL IS BITS 25-31 NOW, NOT 0-7   XA0034DK         
         N     R1,=A(SEGSTLM) WITHOUT THE S BIT                XA0034DK         
./ R 00222700          $ 00222800 100                                           
         SLL   R1,4+8         SEGMENTS, THEN PAGES PER SEG     XA0034DK         
./ R 00241000          $ 00241100 100                                           
*  4088 BYTES OF SLACK, NOT 56: AN ESA/390 SEGMENT TABLE MUST  XA0034DK         
*  BE ON A 4096-BYTE BOUNDARY BECAUSE THE STD'S ORIGIN IS      XA0034DK         
*  BITS 1-19 WITH TWELVE ZEROS APPENDED. DMKBLDRL'S F15        XA0034DK         
*  BECOMES F519 TO MATCH, AND THE TWO MUST BE CHANGED          XA0034DK         
*  TOGETHER OR FRET RETURNS THE WRONG LENGTH.                  XA0034DK         
         AL    R0,=F'511'     PLUS 511 FOR 4096-ALIGNMENT      XA0034DK         
./ R 00243000          $ 00243100 100                                           
         LA    R6,4095(,R1)   ROUND UP -- 4095 IS THE MOST     XA0034DK         
*                             AN LA CAN ENCODE                 XA0034DK         
./ R 00244000          $ 00244100 100                                           
         N     R6,=A(SEGSTOM)      (IN R6)                     XA0034DK         
./ R 00246090          $ 00246091 001                                           
         N     R8,=A(SEGSTOM) STL IS IN THE LOW BITS, SO LA    XA0034DK         
*                             NO LONGER STRIPS IT              XA0034DK         
./ R 00246230          $ 00246240 010                                           
         TM    SEGPTO+3,SEGENQ+SEGINVAL AVAILABLE?             XA0034DK         
./ R 00246270          $ 00246271 001                                           
         L     R0,SEGPTO      THE WHOLE ENTRY                  XA0034DK         
         N     R0,=A(SEGPTOM) (ONLY IF POINTER = 0)            XA0034DK         
./ R 00246370          $ 00246380 010                                           
         A     R1,=A(X'100000') NEXT VIRTUAL SEGMENT           XA0034DK         
./ R 00254000          $ 00254100 100                                           
         N     R8,=A(SEGSTOM) WITHOUT THE LENGTH               XA0034DK         
./ R 00264000          $ 00264100 100                                           
*  STL IS BITS 25-31, SO BYTE 3, NOT BYTE 0. THE VALUE IS      XA0034DK         
*  UNCHANGED: ESA/390 COUNTS THE SEGMENT TABLE IN 64-BYTE      XA0034DK         
*  UNITS MINUS ONE, EXACTLY AS S/370 DID, AND ONLY THE         XA0034DK         
*  MEANING OF A UNIT MOVES -- 1 MB TO 16 MB. SAFE IN BYTE 3    XA0034DK         
*  BECAUSE THE TABLE IS 4096-ALIGNED, SO BITS 20-31 OF THE     XA0034DK         
*  STORED ADDRESS ARE ZERO AND THE S BIT STAYS CLEAR. I-129.   XA0034DK         
         STC   R15,VMSEG+3    AND STORE IN THE STL FIELD.      XA0034DK         
./ R 00287000          $ 00287100 100                                           
ALLNG    LA    R15,SEGINVAL   INVALID STE INDICATOR            XA0034DK         
./ R 00297000          $ 00297100 100                                           
         L     R6,VMSEG       GET SEGTABLE ORIGIN              XA0034DK         
         N     R6,=A(SEGSTOM) NO LENGTH -- LA CANNOT           XA0034DK         
*                             STRIP IT FROM THE LOW BITS       XA0034DK         
./ R 00299000          $ 00299100 100                                           
         SRL   R3,8           DROP THE PAGE NUMBER             XA0034DK         
./ R 00305400          $ 00305410 010                                           
         LA    R4,256         LOAD R4 WITH CONSTANT 256        XA0034DK         
./ R 00308000          $ 00308100 100                                           
BLDRPAGE LA    R4,256         LOAD THE CONSTANT 256            XA0034DK         
./ R 00309100          $ 00309110 010                                           
         L     R15,SEGPTO     IS THERE A PAGTABLE PTR          XA0034DK         
         N     R15,=A(SEGPTOM) ...                             XA0034DK         
./ R 00309305          $ 00309315 010                                           
         TM    SEGPTO+3,SEGINVAL IF NOT, MAKE SURE IT'S        XA0034DK         
./ R 00309700          $ 00309710 010                                           
         TM    SEGPTO+3,SEGENQ IS SEGMENT ENQUEUED?            XA0034DK         
./ R 00321000          $ 00321100 100                                           
         TM    SEGPTO+3,SEGPTLF 256 PAGES IN SEG ALREADY?      XA0034DK         
./ R 00323000          $ 00323100 100                                           
         BO    SKIPBLD        YES - THEN NO NEED TO BUILD      XA0034DK         
./ R 00325000          $ 00325100 100                                           
FORCE16  LA    R5,256         BUILD 256 PAGE TABLE ENTRIES     XA0034DK         
./ R 00327000          $ 00327100 100                                           
         N     R2,=A(SEGSTOM) STRIP LENGTH -- LOW BITS         XA0034DK         
./ R 00332000          $ 00332100 100                                           
         SLL   R1,24          MOVE BEG SEG NUM TO FRET.        XA0034DK         
./ R 00333000          $ 00333100 100                                           
         SLL   R2,8           ENDING SEGMENT NUMBER            XA0034DK         
./ R 00342200          $ 00342210 010                                           
*  SEVEN MORE DOUBLEWORDS SO PAGPFRA CAN BE ROUNDED TO A       XA0034DK         
*  64-BYTE BOUNDARY. AN ESA/390 PAGE TABLE ORIGIN IS BITS      XA0034DK         
*  1-25 WITH SIX ZEROS APPENDED; DMKFREE PROMISES DOUBLEWORDS  XA0034DK         
*  AND NOTHING MORE, AND AN S/370 PAGE TABLE NEEDED ONLY       XA0034DK         
*  EIGHT, WHICH IS WHY THERE WAS NO ROUNDING HERE BEFORE.      XA0034DK         
         SRL   R0,3           OBTAIN NUMBER OF DOUBLEWORDS     XA0034DK         
         AL    R0,F7          PLUS 7 TO ALIGN PAGPFRA TO 64    XA0034DK         
./ R 00343600          $ 00343610 010                                           
*  ROUND THE BLOCK SO THAT PAGPFRA, NOT THE HEADER, LANDS ON   XA0034DK         
*  64. THE DMKFREE ADDRESS GOES IN PAGORIG BELOW, BECAUSE THE  XA0034DK         
*  GAP IS NO LONGER THE CONSTANT 16 THAT DMKBLDRL SUBTRACTS.   XA0034DK         
*  I-130.                                                      XA0034DK         
         LR    R7,R1          DMKFREE ADDRESS                  XA0034DK         
         AL    R7,=A(PAGPFRA-PAGSTMP+63) ROUND UP              XA0034DK         
         N     R7,=A(SEGPTOM) TO A 64-BYTE BOUNDARY            XA0034DK         
         S     R7,=A(PAGPFRA-PAGSTMP) BACK TO HEADER           XA0034DK         
./ R 00346100          $ 00346200 100                                           
         XC    PAGACT(PAGPFRA-PAGACT),PAGACT CLEAR HDR         XA0034DK         
         ST    R1,PAGORIG     EXACT DMKFREE ADDRESS, FOR FRET  XA0034DK         
./ R 00346600 00347100 $ 00346610 010                                           
*  INVALIDATE ALL 256 ENTRIES. THE OLD FORM WAS MVC            XA0034DK         
*  PAGCORE,F8+2 THEN MVC PAGCORE+2(15*2),PAGCORE -- A          XA0034DK         
*  ONE-BYTE-OVERLAP PROPAGATE. 255 FULLWORD ENTRIES IS 1020    XA0034DK         
*  BYTES AND MVC STOPS AT 256, SO IT BECOMES A LOOP. PAGINVW   XA0034DK         
*  IS DERIVED FROM PAGINV, SO IF THE INVALID BIT EVER MOVES    XA0034DK         
*  AGAIN THE FULLWORD FORM FOLLOWS IT.                         XA0034DK         
         LA    R0,256         ENTRIES IN A FULL PAGE TABLE     XA0034DK         
         LA    R2,PAGPFRA     FIRST ENTRY                      XA0034DK         
         L     R15,=A(PAGINVW) AN INVALID PTE                  XA0034DK         
BLDRPTE  ST    R15,0(,R2)     INVALIDATE ONE ENTRY             XA0034DK         
         LA    R2,4(,R2)      NEXT ENTRY                       XA0034DK         
         BCT   R0,BLDRPTE     ALL OF THEM                      XA0034DK         
./ R 00348100          $ 00348200 100                                           
         LA    R2,PAGPFRA     LOAD ADR OF PTE                  XA0034DK         
./ R 00348600 00350600 $ 00348700 100                                           
*  BUILD THE WHOLE ENTRY IN A REGISTER AND STORE IT ONCE.      XA0034DK         
*  BYTE 3 OF AN ESA/390 STE HOLDS PTO BITS 24-25 AS WELL AS    XA0034DK         
*  I, C AND PTL, SO A STC INTO IT WOULD DESTROY PART OF THE    XA0034DK         
*  PAGE TABLE ADDRESS. THE ADDRESS NEEDS NO SHIFTING: PTO IS   XA0034DK         
*  BITS 1-25 WITH SIX ZEROS APPENDED, SO A 64-BYTE-ALIGNED     XA0034DK         
*  ADDRESS IS ALREADY IN PLACE.                                XA0034DK         
         LR    R15,R4         NUMBER OF PAGES LESS ONE         XA0034DK         
         SRL   R15,4          PTL COUNTS 16 ENTRIES AT A TIME  XA0034DK         
         OR    R15,R2         PAGE TABLE ORIGIN, 64-ALIGNED    XA0034DK         
         O     R15,=A(SEGINVAL) NO PAGES IN CORE YET           XA0034DK         
         ST    R15,SEGPTO     ONE STORE, NO READ-MODIFY-WRITE  XA0034DK         
./ R 00351600          $ 00351700 100                                           
         LA    R8,PAGPFRA+256*L'PAGPFRA SWAP TABLE             XA0034DK         
./ R 00372000          $ 00372100 100                                           
SKIPBLD  LA    R6,SEGPTO+4    POINT TO NXT STE                 XA0034DK         
